00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:14.950
Let's go next to Varuna from New Delhi.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.810
Varun, you were on the air.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.730
Oh, hey, David, how are you?

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.680
Well, how are you?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:27.870
I'm doing well, OK,
if I just had a simple question, you know,

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.419
barring for the moment that the minimum wage
increase isn't going to be passed, that it's

00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:37.459
been removed from the relief bill, I mean,
it was removed from the relief bill.

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:46.049
If it had been passed and you eventually got
to a minimum wage, how would that affect the

00:02:46.049 --> 00:02:49.280
minimum wage recipients functional liquidity?

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:55.489
Because if that elevates them beyond the qualification
threshold, like the minimum for, you know,

00:02:55.489 --> 00:03:03.590
I guess broadly welfare benefits, snap benefits
and low income housing, that sort of thing.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.719
I mean, basically all their money is just
going to go back into that stuff.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:12.469
So you argue in favor of demand side stimulus,
but, you know, how does that work out?

00:03:12.469 --> 00:03:18.349
Does it have to be accompanied with other
sort of policies that raise the, you know,

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:20.829
the income threshold to qualify for these
things?

00:03:20.829 --> 00:03:22.200
So this is a great question.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:28.510
And the crux of the question is if you make
nine bucks an hour, but in addition, you qualify

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.040
for certain welfare benefits and then you
have some total income for the year, which

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:38.359
is your nine dollar an hour job, plus maybe
one hundred and eighty bucks a month in food

00:03:38.359 --> 00:03:39.359
stamps.

00:03:39.359 --> 00:03:42.010
You add it all together and then you say,
OK, we're going to give you fifteen dollars

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.010
an hour.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:48.359
But as a result of that, you will exceed the
income threshold for some of these benefits.

00:03:48.359 --> 00:03:49.699
Do you really come out ahead?

00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:52.000
That's the crux of your question, right?

00:03:52.000 --> 00:04:00.909
Yeah, basically, yeah, it's a it's a very
fair question, the answer is it depends significantly

00:04:00.909 --> 00:04:06.959
on what's going on at the state level in many,
which is which is different from for many

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:08.010
people.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.170
But you have to account for a couple of different
things.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:17.739
One is, is a 15 dollar minimum wage, for example,
like Alabama has no state minimum wage.

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:21.739
So in Alabama or maybe it's Mississippi, maybe
it's both the minimum wage and some of these

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:23.230
states is the federal, which is seven.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.230
Twenty five.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:25.830
So 15 is more than doubling.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.250
The impact there on eligibility for programs
is going to be very different than in a state

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.330
that already has an eleven dollar minimum
wage and it goes to fifteen.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.670
And that's going to vary state by state.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.890
You also have to remember that a lot of people
who qualify for benefits don't actually go

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:45.630
through the process of getting them because
the they either don't know that the benefits

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:50.930
are available or the system is cumbersome
or complicated or whatever the case may be.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.320
So while there's no question that there are
some people who will get a raise from a minimum

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:01.670
wage increase and they'll lose something on
the welfare side, when you account for the

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:06.550
difference in money in the pocket versus a
housing subsidy, money in the pocket versus

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:12.440
food stamps, people who don't understand or
avail themselves of these systems, the net

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:17.540
benefit is still significant, but that doesn't
mean what you're saying doesn't exist.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.290
And I think it's important to consider it.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:21.120
Oh, OK, thanks.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.630
All right, no problem.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:28.470
